Dear Ms.Kincade,
Enclosed with this letter please find theliquor license application fortheF&G Corporation owned
theF&G Corporation and the liquor license and tolet the Clerk's office knowl intend to park the license
at my current place of business(address below)for the time being and hope to sell the license before
July 18, 2025.
The Liquor License is currently listed for sale in the Cheyenne, MLS and Ihave parked the licenseatmy
business office,255Storey Blvd, Cheyenne, WY82009.A copy of the MLS listing is enclosed with this
letter and the application.
Leslie W.Gallion, the longtime owner(~50 years)ofthe F&G Corporation and managerof The Green
Door passed away on July 16th,2024. As his landlord for the past 5years, Les and1had many discussions
and had become friends.As Les got older, he indicated that his business was not doing well and that Les
Green Door.In order to keep Les solvent and allow Les to live out the remainder of his lifewithout
money concerns, Iagreed to buy the Liquor License over athree-yearperiod, startingin2023with two
additional payments in2024and2025.
Unfortunately, Les died during the first year of our agreement.Since Les'sdeath, I have made the
second payment on the Liquor License and Iam now the majority(66.67%)owner with Les'sestate
owning the remaining 33.33%.If the license has not sold by the end of 2025, Iwill make thefinal
payment to Les's estate andbe the sole owner of the license.After Lespassed away, we were forced to
boardup and close The Green doorandI was informed by the Wyoming Liquor Division thatwehave
started a one year“non-operational time”allowed by the division.The buildinghas subsequently sold
so wedo not currently have a location for operating the liquor license.
If thelicense does not sell before July,182025, I will askforan extension from the cityin ordertofind a
